writing:{
 title:'Task 1 – Line graph',
 prompt:'The line graph below shows the percentage of teenagers in a city who used three types of online platforms between 2016 and 2024. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant. Write at least 150 words.',
 chart:{type:'line',title:'Teenagers using online platforms (%)',unit:'% of teenagers',cats:['2016','2018','2020','2022','2024'],series:['Video-sharing apps','Messaging apps','Social networking sites'],data:[[20,35,50,70,80],[50,54,57,62,63],[75,70,65,48,40]]},
 min:150,max:190,
 outline:['Mở bài: paraphrase (shows → illustrates; teenagers → young people).','Overview: video-sharing tăng mạnh và cao nhất cuối kỳ; social networking giảm đều; messaging tăng nhẹ.','Thân bài 1: hai đường thay đổi lớn — video-sharing (20 → 80, vượt social networking) và social networking (75 → 40).','Thân bài 2: messaging apps (50 → 62, đi ngang ở 63).'],
 model:'The line graph <b>illustrates</b> the percentage of teenagers in a city who used three types of online platforms between 2016 and 2024.<br><br><i>Overall</i>, video-sharing apps grew dramatically and became the most popular type of platform, <i>whereas</i> social networking sites declined steadily. Messaging apps <b>rose</b> only gradually over the period.<br><br>In 2016, social networking sites were the most widely used, at 75%, while only 20% of teenagers used video-sharing apps. <i>However</i>, the figure for video-sharing apps <b>rose rapidly</b>, <b>overtaking</b> social networking sites between 2020 and 2022, and it <b>peaked at</b> 80% in 2024. <i>By contrast</i>, the use of social networking sites fell continuously to just 40% at the end of the period.<br><br>Messaging apps followed a more stable pattern. Their popularity increased gradually from 50% in 2016 to 62% in 2022 and then <b>levelled off</b> at 63% in 2024. <i>As a result</i>, they ranked second in the final year.',
 note:'153 từ, band 6.0. Overview không có số liệu. Thân bài 1 nhóm hai đường biến động mạnh và có so sánh (overtaking); thân bài 2 là đường ổn định.',
 checklist:['Mở bài paraphrase','Overview nêu xu hướng chính, không số liệu','Có dùng ít nhất 3 từ: peak, overtake, level off, fluctuate, steadily','Có so sánh giữa các đường','Ít nhất 150 từ']
},
speaking:{
 task:'Ghi âm bài nói Part 2 (đủ 1,5–2 phút) và 2 câu Part 3, gửi cô qua Zalo.',
 items:[
 ['How often do you use the internet?','Every day, to be honest. I use it to look up information for my homework, and in the evening I usually chat with friends or watch videos.'],
 ['What apps do you use most?',"I use messaging apps the most, because that's how my class shares homework and news. I also use a dictionary app quite often for English."],
 ['Do you think you spend too much time on your phone?','Probably yes. Some days I spend more than three hours on it, so now I turn off notifications when I study.'],
 ['Did you use computers at primary school?','Only a little. We had one computer lesson a week, and we mostly learned how to type and draw simple pictures.']],
 part2:{cue:'Describe a useful app or website you often use.',bullets:['what it is','how you found out about it','what you use it for','and explain why you find it useful.'],
  notes:'dictionary app · teacher recommended (2 years ago) · homework, reading, save word lists · saves time, pronunciation button',
  model:"I'd like to talk about a dictionary app that I use almost every day. It's a free English–Vietnamese dictionary, and I found out about it two years ago when my English teacher recommended it to our class. I mainly use it when I'm doing homework or reading articles in English. Whenever I see a new word, I type it in, and the app shows me the meaning, the pronunciation and several example sentences. There's also a feature that lets me save words into lists, so I can review them later before tests. The reason I find it so useful is that it saves me a lot of time. In the past, I had to look up words in a thick paper dictionary, which was slow and quite boring. Now I can check a word in a few seconds, even when I'm on the bus. Another thing I like is the pronunciation button, because I can listen to native speakers and copy them, which has helped me speak more clearly. Overall, I think this app has made a big difference to my English, and I would definitely recommend it to other students who want to improve their vocabulary."},
 part3:[
 ['Why do young people spend so much time on social media?',"I think the main reason is that social media is designed to be entertaining, so it's easy to keep scrolling. Also, teenagers want to stay connected with their friends and know what's happening, so they check their phones very often."],
 ['Should parents control how their children use technology?',"To some extent, yes. Younger children don't always understand the risks online, so parents should set some limits. However, for teenagers, I think talking about responsible use works better than strict rules, because they need to learn to manage their own time."],
 ['How might technology change education in the future?','I believe lessons will become more personalised. For example, apps could check what each student finds difficult and give them suitable exercises. But teachers will still be important, because students need someone to motivate and guide them.']]
},
